      "entry_id": "POD-DHAGA-007",
      "style": "line art",
      "brief": "A single broad thundercloud in loose black ink above quiet bare ground, a few angular sound marks around the cloud, no raindrops. Warm off-white page, generous empty space, no lettering, no ornate border. Keep the weather scene spare; no documentary claim about monsoon behaviour.",
      "caption": "Thunder fills the air; the ground stays dry.",
      "alt": "An ink-drawn thundercloud hangs over dry ground without releasing rain.",
      "basis": "Existing meaning contrasts noisy promises with action. Metaphor, not a meteorological rule."
    },
    {
      "entry_id": "POD-DHAGA-104",
      "style": "line art",
      "brief": "Two anatomically credible hands facing each other just before a clap, wrists entering from opposite lower corners. Simple expressive black pen contours, five fingers per hand, warm paper, no jewellery, costume, text or gesture associated with prayer. Hands belong to a shared action, not a dispute.",
      "caption": "A clap needs two palms to meet.",
      "alt": "Two open palms face each other just before a clap.",
      "basis": "Existing entry invites cooperation and expressly does not equate the blame of two parties."
    },
    {
      "entry_id": "POD-DHAGA-081",
      "style": "heritage-inspired ink and wash",
      "brief": "An openly imaginative winter vignette on textured warm paper: a curling blue-grey gust resolves into the outline of a tiger beside a plain shawl folded on a low stool. Restrained charcoal and faded indigo with a small ochre accent. Tiger should be part of the wind, not a real animal threatening a village. No temple, deity, costume shorthand, fake archival lettering or claimed traditional painting lineage.",
      "caption": "Winter’s bite takes the shape of a tiger.",
      "alt": "A cold blue-grey gust curls into a tiger shape beside a folded shawl.",
      "basis": "Existing Magha saying compares the severity of cold to a tiger; visual metaphor only, no claim about animal behaviour or historical dress."
    },
    {
      "entry_id": "POD-DHAGA-106",
      "style": "heritage-inspired colour illustration",
      "brief": "One small imagined flower with a fine stem suspended in a wide empty sky above a distant quiet horizon. Its stem touches neither soil nor water: the missing support is the central idea. Hand-worked ink and restrained dusty rose, indigo and ochre washes on warm paper, calm rather than magical spectacle. No recognizable religious lotus emblem, deity, temple or imitation archival inscription.",
      "caption": "A beautiful flower, with nowhere to take root.",
      "alt": "A flower hangs in empty sky, its stem ending above the distant ground.",
      "basis": "Existing figurative compound questions a plan’s real foundation, not imagination itself."
    }
  ],
